/* ============================================================================
   STATE REGISTER — section 1 of the cover sheet, one row per office.
   ============================================================================

   Picking an office on the opening screen fills in the whole letterhead from
   the matching row below: the trading entity, its ABN/ACN, contact details and
   the default letter wording. Nothing here comes from SharePoint — these
   details change once a year, not once a project, so they ship with the app and
   work with no network and no flow configured.

   Mostly one row per Australian state, but not necessarily: NZ is a row too.
   The rows are keyed by `code`, and `state` is simply what the SharePoint
   column holding that code is called.

   TO EDIT: change the values below, or use Settings -> State register in the
   app (which writes your edits to this browser and, if you click Export,
   gives you a replacement copy of this file to commit).

   Fields, all optional except `entity`:
     code      the office's abbreviation; also the key used to filter the
               SharePoint project register, so it must match the State column
               there exactly
     name      spelled out, shown on the picker tile
     entity    registered company name, prints as the letterhead heading
     abn/acn   shown as their own letterhead rows when set, hidden when blank —
               which is how an entity without one gets a clean letterhead
               rather than one reading "ABN: N/A"
     phone     letterhead + signature block
     address   letterhead; newlines are preserved
     email     letterhead + signature block
     logo      optional data: URL or path to an image, overrides the shared logo
     intro     default opening line of the letter
     closing   default closing line
============================================================================ */

